# .claudeignore — context-window noise filter (AUTONOMY_HACKS.md Параметр 1 #13)
#
# NOT a security boundary and NOT a build-context filter (that's
# .dockerignore, which stays separate and stricter). This file exists
# purely so an autonomous agent doesn't burn its context window reading
# generated artifacts, caches, or binary blobs that carry no information
# per token. When genuinely investigating one of these paths (e.g.
# debugging a specific coverage gap in htmlcov/), read it explicitly by
# path — this file only affects broad/exploratory reads (tree walks, glob
# searches), not a direct Read call on a named file.

# Python bytecode & caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Coverage artifacts (regenerate via `pytest --cov`, never hand-edit)
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
*.cover

# Virtual environments / dependency trees (equivalent of node_modules)
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Logs and runtime data (this project's DATA_DIR contents)
*.log
logs/
data/maps/
data/profiles/
data/objects/

# Point cloud / binary data blobs (large, non-token-dense, read via a
# script/loader when actually needed, never by pasting into context)
*.ply
*.pcd
*.h5
*.npy
*.npz

# Version control internals
.git/
.gitignore

# IDE / OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Compiled / packaged output
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.whl
*.tar.gz

# Lock files (content is machine-generated pin data, not something an
# agent should read line-by-line to reason about; check for EXISTENCE and
# top-level version conflicts instead, per AUTONOMY_HACKS.md Токен-
# эффективность #2)
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
poetry.lock

# Scratch/temp directories an agent may create for itself
/tmp/
scratch/
*.tmp

# Large generated docs/dumps that are regenerated, not hand-authored
# (context_map.json is the one exception -- it's small, curated, and IS
# meant to be read; keep it OUT of this list)
